# rm180, the coin-biter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm180
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_hilde_rainmore
written_by claude
title the coin-biter
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk bites_every_coin_to_see_if_it_is_true
likes crisp_apples stars old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes waiting gulls
fears a_bad_coin_in_the_till being_fooled_in_front_of_everyone
hopes a_map_with_no_mistakes_on_it to_count_every_star
topics pastimes +0.4 prices +0.3 weather +0.3 family +0.2 season +0.3 gossip +0.2 player -0.3
styles comfort=bossy gossip=keen refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# talks loud and fast, trusts nobody until proven, bites every coin that comes near to see if it is true, hunts the wrong roads on old maps, and is forever counting the stars.

words
oath! = Gold or tin | Teeth and tin
saying! = If it bends, it's bad | Bite first, believe after
coin = a coin | a coin I haven't bitten yet
truegold = true gold | gold that gives a little when you bite it
oldmap = an old map | a map so old the lanes have moved
stars = the stars | every star over the roofs
apple = a crisp apple | an apple with no worm in it
warmday = the first warm day | the first day you don't need a scarf
waiting = waiting | standing about waiting on folk
gulls = gulls | those screaming gulls
floodstreet = the bottom lanes | the bottom lanes, where the water comes first
prove = Prove it | Show me, then
hah = Hah | Ha

any
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : Festival's when the street's all out and loud, and nobody says hush to me. | Festivals are best. I count the lanterns. Last time, ninety-four.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : New faces get no trust from me. That's just sense. | Strangers smile too much. I watch their paws, not their faces.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : Folk stand in that queue all morning. They could be doing something. That's what I think. | The dole line goes right past our shop. Nobody buys a ring in it.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Ridgemere's the biggest city. I've seen it on a map. Three maps, and two were wrong. | Born in Ridgemere, stopping in Ridgemere. I know where everything floods.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : Some shopkeepers are honest and some give you light coins. I check. | You have to bite their money. Not all of it. The shiny ones.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The Watch walk past our door twice a night. I count. Sometimes it's once. | I told a watchman a coin was bad and he didn't believe me. It was bad.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Paws off the counter. | #greet#. Quick, I'm busy.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Don't know you. I'll know you better by the time you've paid. | #greet#. New face. I'll be watching.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Honest still, I hope. | #greet#. I was counting.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Watch the bottom lanes if it rains. | #farewell#. And bite your change.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Uphill route home, mind.
line @1 react.news : Go on. All of it. | Who's saying so? Go on.
line @1 react.news.new : That's news. I usually hear first. | #oath#. Nobody told me.
line @1 react.news.known : Knew that. Customers had it. | Old. Two days, that.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #prove#. Unbitten news I don't swallow. | Somebody's polished that story. Polished things fool folk.
line @1 answer.how : Busy, and short of patience. | Fair. I've had worse days. Not many.
line @1 decline : I won't. It smells wrong, and I don't go near what smells wrong. | No. Not without seeing proof first, and you've none.
line @1 accept_decline : Suit yourself. | Fine. Your loss.
line @1 thank : Thanks. Don't expect it to make me soft. | Thank you. I'll remember. I remember everything.
line @1 preclose : Counting waits for nobody. Off with you. | Can't stand here all day.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Right. Off you go.
scene gr_coin
when topic=prices|work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Still bite every coin. I've caught more bad money than the Watch. | A tin coin came over the counter today. I bit it, and they went white.
b : Your teeth must be iron. | Serves them right.
a : Near enough. Gold gives; tin doesn't; teeth know. | It does. Bite first, that's my way.

scene gr_coin_honest
when topic=smalltalk|prices
does give.opinion / disagree / insist
a : Most folk are honest, they say. Most folk haven't bitten as many coins as me. | I trust what I've bitten. That's coins. Folk, I trust slower.
b : You're too hard on people. | That's a bleak way to live.
a : I'm right on people. That's different. | It's a safe way. Bleak and safe.

scene gr_maps
when topic=pastimes|lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Every map of Ridgemere I've seen has a lane wrong. I've stopped being angry. Nearly. | I keep a map of my own. Every bend right, and the flood streets marked.
b : Who'd make a map wrong on purpose? | Flood streets marked?
a : Nobody. They just never walked it. I have. | In blue. The bottom lanes go first, every time.

scene gr_stars
when topic=pastimes here.time=night here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Clear night. I still count the stars. Never finished. Never will. | I like a clear night. The stars don't lie about where they are.
b : What number are you up to? | Don't they?
a : I lost count at a thousand and something. I start again each time. | They're the only thing that doesn't. That's why I like them.

scene gr_flood
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Keep off #floodstreet#. Another hour of this and they're under. | It's coming down. The bottom lanes will be ankle-deep by dusk.
b : You always know. | How can you tell?
a : Years of watching. Nobody else bothers. | The gutters by the wharf. When they bubble, it's coming.

scene gr_waiting
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Stood an hour at the gate for a cart. It never came. Never again. | Waiting. Hated it as a pup, hate it now. Folk say it's patience. It's just standing.
b : Annoying, that. | Patience is a virtue.
a : Worse than annoying. An hour's an hour. | It's a waste. That's what it is.

scene gr_gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Gull took a pie off a sill this morning. The whole pie. | I'll never forgive gulls. Loud, greedy and never sorry.
b : Cheeky beggars. | Never sorry, no.
a : Robbers. Feathered robbers. | Not once. I'd bite them if I could.

scene gr_apples
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A crisp apple. Turned over twice, no holes, then eaten. That's the way. | Bought six apples. Checked every one. One had a worm. Took it back.
b : Thorough. | Did they swap it?
a : Worms don't knock. You have to look. | They did, once I showed them the hole.

scene gr_spring
when topic=season here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #warmday.capitalize#. Scarf off. Best day there is. | Warm at last. The steps hold the sun and I sat on them an hour.
b : Spring's welcome. | An hour?
a : About time. | An hour. Didn't even mind the waiting, for once.

scene gr_gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Maybe true. Haven't bitten it yet. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm passing it on as I got it.
b : You don't believe it? | Hm.
a : I believe they said it. That's all I'll swear to. | That's all I know. Weigh it yourself.

scene gr_strangers
when topic=player|newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Somebody new in the lane. Smiles a lot. I'll be watching that one. | That traveller paid with good coin. I bit it. I like them a bit more now.
b : Give them a chance. | A bit?
a : I am. One chance. I'm watching it. | A bit. Coins are coins; folk are harder.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? Quick. | #greet#. Say it plain.
dlg @5 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You've been honest so far. | #topic.player#. Back. Good coin last time.
dlg @6 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late. Quick about it. | Late. What?
dlg @7 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it from there. I'm watching your paws. | Hm. Go on, then.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. And I check every coin that comes near me. | Work. I do it right.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Not bitten it yet. | Heard that #world.news#. Out of #world.news_from#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# today. | Everybody's on about #world.event_words#.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : A wagon's been robbed outside the walls. Stay in, I would. | Thieves took a cart, outside the walls. Watch your coin.
dlg @4 resident.news [world.death=recent] : Somebody on our street's died. It's gone quiet. | There's been a death. Folk are low.
dlg @5 resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : There was a wedding. Somebody's happy. | Somebody got wed. Forty-one guests; I counted.
dlg @6 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Nothing worth biting. | Nothing new. I'd know.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Unbitten, mind. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Nothing. And I'd know.
dlg @2 resident.bye : #farewell#. Bite your change. | #farewell#. Uphill way, if it's wet.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#! Busy, but you can stand there. | #greet#. Don't touch anything, I've just tidied it.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Not seen you before. My eyes are on you, so behave. | Who are you? Don't say, I won't believe it anyway. #greet#.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : #greet#. Keep off the bottom lanes, they're under already. | #greet#! It's raining. The bottom street's flooding, I can tell.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Guess what I bit today. A real one! | You're late. I've been waiting for ages, and I hate waiting.
line @1 again.open : You again! I'm still busy. | Back already. I'm counting, so be quiet a moment.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! You can talk, I'm listening with one ear. | #greet#. I'm doing something important. It's a secret.
line @1 farewell : Bye! Don't take any bad money. | Bye. Mind the bottom lanes if it rains.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye! | Bye. Go the high way.
line @1 react.news : What? Properly, now, the beginning first. | Who told you? I want names. Well, not names. Tell me.
line @1 react.news.new : I didn't know that! I know everything, usually. | #oath#! Nobody tells me anything first.
line @1 react.news.known : I knew that already. Everybody at lessons knows. | Old news. I heard it ages ago, before breakfast.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #prove#. I don't believe it till I see it. | That's a fib. I can always tell a fib.
line @1 answer.how : Busy. I've three things to do and nobody's helping. | Good. I bit a coin and it was true. Best day.
line @1 thank : Thank you. I'll check it later, mind. | Thanks. It's not bad, is it?
line @1 decline : No. Not allowed, and I'd say no anyhow. That's twice no. | I won't. You're too new, and new folk get no yes from me.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. Somebody else will. | All right. You're missing out.
line @1 ack : #hah# | Mm-hm.
rule @young_coin
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Is that a real coin? Give it here, I'll bite it. | #saying#. That's the rule. My rule.

rule @young_wait
when concept=bark self.dislikes=waiting
does aside
cooldown 8h
say How long now? I've been waiting forever. | Hurry up! Everybody's so slow!

rule @young_gulls
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Go away, gull! Shoo! Nobody likes you! | That gull took somebody's pie. I saw. Thief!

scene yg_bite_coin
when topic=prices|smalltalk
does tell.boast / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I bite every coin I get. If it's true gold it gives a little. If it's tin it doesn't. | Somebody paid with a funny coin today. I bit it. Tin. I told everyone.
b : Doesn't it hurt your teeth? | What happened then?
a : A bit. I've got strong teeth. Stronger than a coin. | They went red and paid with a proper one. I was right.
b? : #bc_clever# | #bc_ha#

scene yg_bite_more
when topic=prices|family self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the coins at our counter. Nobody's better at it. #self.mother# would say so too, I bet. | I found a bad coin in the till. I hope #self.mother# heard it was me. I already know I'm clever.
b : That's an important job. | Very clever.
a : It's the most important job. Without me they'd be full of tin. | I know. I said so.

scene yg_old_map
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've got an old map. Half the roads are in the wrong place. Whoever drew it never walked it. | I found a mistake on a map in the schoolroom. A street that isn't there. I told the teacher.
b : Old maps are like that. | What did the teacher say?
a : Then they should say so on the map. In big letters. | Said I was right and to sit down. I sat down. I was still right.

scene yg_map_wrong
when topic=pastimes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Maps say the river goes straight. It doesn't. It goes wiggly. I've walked it. | No map has our street on it right. It shows it straight. It bends twice.
b : Maybe it was straight once. | You should draw a better one.
a : Rivers don't move. Well, they don't move much. | I'm going to. When I've got enough paper.

scene yg_stars
when topic=pastimes|weather here.time=night here.weather=clear
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I'm counting the stars. I got to two hundred last night before I fell asleep. | Grown-ups say you can't count the stars. I can. I just haven't finished.
b : Two hundred! Which one's the brightest? | And when will you be done?
a : The one over the chapel. It's always first. I watch for it. | Years, maybe. That's fine. Stars can wait for me.
b? : #bc_go_on# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene yg_apple
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a crisp apple. But I look at it all over first, for holes. Worms make holes. | Got an apple off the cart. I checked it twice. No worm. Then I ate it, crunch, crunch.
b : Very thorough. | Good apple?
a : You have to be. Worms don't tell you they're there. | Best one this week. I've had five.

scene yg_waiting
when topic=day|smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I hate waiting. I waited for the bread queue and it took a whole forever. | Grown-ups always say "in a minute". It's never a minute. I counted. It was a hundred.
b : Waiting's part of life. | They do say that.
a : It shouldn't be. Somebody should fix it. | A hundred and four. I'm telling everybody.

scene yg_flood
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Don't go down the bottom lanes. They go under first. Then the steps by the wharf. Then the square. | I know which streets flood. I sit at our window and see. #floodstreet.capitalize# always go first.
b : How do you know all that? | Thanks for telling me.
a : I watch. Each rain, I watch. Nobody else does. | You're welcome. Don't say I didn't tell you.

scene yg_gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Gulls are thieves. One took a whole fish off a cart and the carter just shouted. | I shouted at a gull and it shouted back. It wasn't sorry at all.
b : They're cheeky things. | Gulls are never sorry.
a : They're worse than cheeky. They're robbers with feathers. | Never. That one's on my list of thieves.

scene yg_warm_day
when topic=season|weather here.season=spring here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #warmday.capitalize#! Scarf off, and not one grown-up said a word. | It's warm! The steps are warm. I sat on them and they were warm all the way through.
b : Spring's finally here. | Lovely, isn't it.
a : I'm not wearing my scarf again till winter. Not even if they make me. | It is. Best one yet. I'm keeping count.

scene yg_father_door
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like standing at the door with #self.father# and checking who comes in. Some customers look shifty. | I stand by #self.father# at the door and stare at the customers' paws. Paws tell you everything.
b : Shifty how? | What do paws tell you?
a : They look at the rings too long. And they don't buy. | If they're clean, if they're shaking, if they're hiding something. Mostly hiding.

scene yg_friend_kin
when topic=friends|family self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# runs up the stairs and I count the steps. Somebody has to count. | Me and #self.friend# play shops. I'm the one who checks the money.
b : That's a good game. | Who wins?
a : I always know who's winning. It's whoever I say. | Me. Because I check the money.

scene yg_gossip_keen
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Guess what I heard? #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's the talk. | I heard grown-ups talking. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. Nobody saw me.
b : Are you sure? | You shouldn't listen in.
a : I'm sure it got said. True's another thing. | I wasn't listening. I was just standing there with my ears.

story yg_story_tin [topic=memories|prices]
  : A big wolf came in the shop and paid with a shiny coin.
  : I bit it right there. It didn't give at all. It was tin with paint on.
  ask : Guess what the big wolf did next?
  b : Ran off, I'd guess.
  : Ran right out the door. #saying#. Everybody says I'm a hero now. Well, I say it.

story yg_story_map [topic=pastimes]
  : I followed an old map to find a well. I walked and walked.
  : There wasn't a well. There was a bakery. The map was older than the bakery.
  b : Did you get a bun, at least?
  : I got a bun. So the map was a bit right.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Don't touch the window, I just cleaned it. | #greet#. New face. Quick, then, what's wanted?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You paid with a true coin last time. I didn't forget. | #topic.player#! I bit your coin last time. It was real.
dlg @1 resident.job : Lessons. And checking coins. That's my real job. | Sums at school. And I know every street that floods, in order.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Bye! No bad coins! | Bye. The bottom lanes go under when it rains, so don't.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you bite coins? -> bite
node bite
say To see if they're true. True gold gives a little, like a soft apple. Tin doesn't give at all. Want me to bite yours?
mood keen
free
choice No thank you. -> bite_no
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node bite_no
say Then I'll have to trust you. I don't trust anybody. You'd better be honest.
choice I am. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Make it quick, I've an errand for the shop. | #greet#. I was just counting something.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. Keep your coins honest. | Bye, then. Take the high streets.
line @1 react.news.new : Didn't know that. Who said? All of it, now. | #oath#. That's new, and little gets past me.
line @1 answer.how : Busy. Bit three coins today. All true. | Fine. Bored of waiting for things.
rule @teen_coin
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give it here. One bite and I'll know. | Bite first, believe after. Always.

scene ad_coins_counter
when topic=prices|work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sorting coins for the counter now. I can tell tin by the sound before I bite it. | Caught another bad coin last week. They don't try it on me twice.
b : That's a sharp ear. | They'd better not.
a : Sharper than anybody's in the shop. | They don't. Word gets round.

scene ad_maps
when topic=pastimes|lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm drawing a map of the Commons. The right way. Every bend. | Corrected an old map in the schoolroom. In pencil. The teacher hasn't noticed yet.
b : Can I see it when it's done? | You'll get told off.
a : When it's done. It's never done. Ridgemere keeps moving. | It's not wrong to fix a wrong thing.

scene ad_stars
when topic=pastimes here.time=night here.weather=clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I still count the stars. I'm past a thousand now, I think. I lose my place. | Climbed out on the roof after supper and counted till the cold got me.
b : You'll never finish. | On the roof?
a : Maybe not. I'll get further than anybody. | Don't tell. The roof's the best place.

story ad_story_watchman [topic=crime|memories]
  : I told a watchman a coin was bad. He laughed at me.
  : Next week a whole bag of them turned up in the market. Tin, every one.
  b : Did he come back and say sorry?
  : No. But he looks at me different now. That's nearly sorry.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#. Quick, I've errands. | #greet#. Show me your coin first. Only joking. Mostly.
